# Walkthrough - UI & Diarization Polish

## Changes Implemented

### 1. Transcript Display Enhancements
Updated [TranscriptView.tsx](file:///C:/Users/prakh/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/speechmatics-realtime-app/src/components/TranscriptView.tsx) to solve the ambiguity between Channel Labels and Speaker IDs.
- **Before**: Only showed one or the other, or mixed them unpredictably.
- **After**: Clearly shows `Label (Speaker ID)` (e.g., "Interviewer (S1)") when both are present.
- **Styling**: Upgraded to a modern, chat-bubble aesthetic with distinct colors for different speakers.

### 2. Premium UI Polish
Refined [ControlPanel.tsx](file:///C:/Users/prakh/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/speechmatics-realtime-app/src/components/ControlPanel.tsx) to match modern design standards.
- **Visuals**: Added glassmorphism effects (`backdrop-blur`), subtle gradients, and soft shadows.
- **Interactivity**: Added a pulsing animation to the "Stop Transcription" button to clearly indicate active recording.
- **Feedback**: Improved validation warnings for microphone selection conflicts.

### 3. Resilience
Improved [useSpeechmatics.ts](file:///C:/Users/prakh/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/speechmatics-realtime-app/src/lib/useSpeechmatics.ts) channel mapping.
- Added explicit warnings if channel mapping fails (e.g., if Speechmatics doesn't return a channel ID in a multi-channel session), helping with debugging.

